## SAGA exit criteria

S03-001 may establish the packet baseline used by later runtime work. SAGA-03 completes only when S03-002 also verifies GTOC-7 preservation and terminalization for finite migration bundles and both sprints are human promoted; this re-entry does not add a cyclic SAGA prerequisite.

## Surviving obstructions

* GTOC-7/S03-002 remains blocked on GTOC-6 terminal receipts and separate host admission.
* S03-001 proves one finite source closure and exact write lease, not arbitrary packet families or migration preservation.
* No live conductor host, workspace mutation, gate activation, human promotion, or autonomous successor consumes the S03-001 receipt.
* SAGA-03 remains `BLOCKED` until the later S03-002 re-entry terminalizes; the S03-001 `ExactRepair` does not transfer to S03-002.
